  "articleBody": "Knowing when to call in the pros for an accessible closet modification can be tricky, but there are some pretty clear signs it’s time to act. For starters, if simply getting dressed or putting things away has become a daily struggle because of high shelves or hard-to-reach rods, that's a big red flag. Another key indicator is if your current closet layout doesn't allow for comfortable movement, especially if you use a wheelchair or other mobility device and find yourself constantly bumping into things or unable to turn. If you're battling with swing doors that restrict space, or if the hardware on your drawers and closet doors is difficult to grasp, those are definite signals that an upgrade is in order. Essentially, anytime your closet feels like it’s creating barriers rather than providing ease, it's a good idea to consider professional help. HH Remodeling LLC specializes in these kinds of modifications, and we can help transform your closet into a truly functional and user-friendly space that supports your independence and daily routine.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}